{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1308852-hiding-an-omen","id":1308852,"title":"Hiding an Omen","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-04-29T18:30:32-07:00","id":1308852,"title":"Hiding an Omen","content":"Hi everyone. I was just wondering if there's anything I may have missed regarding the omen you develop at Legend 3. My players aren't there yet, but one of them has put a question to me and I didn't have a solid answer and couldn't find one in the RAW.<br /> <br /> The question comes from a player doing amazing (and frustrating!) things with the Deception purview. He's a scion of Loki and also has Fire (which he is also doing amazing, and frustrating) things with and he's decided that his omen is going to be a corona of flames about his hair when he channels or imbues Legend. And that's all well and good but he's, fairly rightly, asked me how he's going to be able to spin subtle and epic lies at that point &quot;when he's lighting up like a bonfire&quot;.<br /> <br /> I couldn't find anything in the RAW that states that an omen is optional, and I'm happy to say that the omen is a sign of a scion's growing divinity and a moving away from their mortal status, but it's certainly going to make his specialty power hard to use discreetly, which is kind of its whole point. I'm kind of happy to rule that Deception, being inherently deceptive (it's in the name!) is a sneaky exception by its very nature but did I miss a passage somewhere that says that an omen can be dampened or hidden? If so would anyone mind pointing it out?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T18:40:42-07:00","id":1308854,"title":"","content":"While, i would'nt allow for an Omen to be hidden. I would allow one to be either not centered on the scion manifesting it or it manifesting in a way subtle enough that people don't immediately associate the Omen to a specific person present there.<br /> In your scion of Loki example, i would go that the reflection of the scion has fiery hair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-29T18:52:46-07:00","id":1308855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maitrecorbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/1308852-hiding-an-omen?p=1308854#post1308854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In your scion of Loki example, i would go that the reflection of the scion has fiery hair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. That's gold. A wonderful idea. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Glad I didn't miss a mention in the rules, then. Killer idea. Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2608-squee","name":"Squee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2608_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"120"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T12:21:34-07:00","id":1309252,"title":"","content":"My Loki Scion has an Omen of &quot;The scent of roses fills the air around her&quot;. Given that she's a conwoman who needs to keep her identities secret, that kind of tell is a bit vexxing to her, so she's been trying to make a line of perfume that smells like her and mass release it. That way she has a cover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-01T13:20:13-07:00","id":1309269,"title":"","content":"As a ST I would go for a no hiding omens, it\u2019s a part of the character and a part of the fun in the game. You could limit the use of some marvels to a lower level or some restriction as a \u201cside omen\u201d. Let\u2019s say the omen is a fiery hair can just be some lights that show up when using with a lower scale, and more like fire when used on a legend 3+ scale.<br /> <br /> I had an Aberrant that were self proclaimed a angel, with healing powers, wings and a \u201choly bolt\u201d. The Anima aberration he had was an halo of light, and it gave him lots of problems but gave also a lot of fun to the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}